; A sale at a fixated cost that names a lot its account holds,
; `-10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] @ =$6`, sells from that lot: Assets:Broker
; is left empty, and print writes the lot as the posting names it, {$5}.
; `@ =price` fixates the lot its own cost creates, as writing {=price}
; would, and never a lot the posting names.
;
; 3.4.1 fixated the named lot itself, for every holder and from its
; purchase on, so the purchase showed as {=$5} [2020/01/01], and print
; wrote the sale as `-10 AAPL @ $6`, without its lot or its `=`, which
; reads back as a sale of another lot, {$6} [2020/02/01]: Assets:Broker
; keeps both lots, and the $10 gain is lost.

2020/01/01 Buy
    Assets:Broker    10 AAPL @ $5
    Assets:Cash

2020/02/01 Sell
    Assets:Broker   -10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] @ =$6
    Assets:Cash      $60
    Income:Gains

test bal --lots
                 $10  Assets:Cash
                $-10  Income:Gains
--------------------
                   0
end test

test print
2020/01/01 Buy
    Assets:Broker                            10 AAPL @ $5
    Assets:Cash

2020/02/01 Sell
    Assets:Broker                       -10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] @= $6
    Assets:Cash                                  $60
    Income:Gains
end test
